From abf5a462fef970b7a7bd631dd55a02f216b8ad6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 14:18:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(int4-gemm): opt-in BF16-output GEMV/GEMM variants for
 mixed-precision

Add gemv_forward_cuda_new_bf16 and gemm_forward_cuda_new_bf16 alongside the
existing FP16 paths (untouched). The BF16 variants reduce/accumulate in FP32
and store BF16, preventing FP16 overflow (>65504 -> inf) for overflow-prone
linears (e.g. down_proj output channel ~2.3e5). GEMV templates the output
store dtype; GEMM adds an FP32-accumulate mma (f32.f16.f16.f32) clone with a
BF16-packed epilogue. Shared-memory staging stays FP16, so smem sizing is
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013XsZpWRubKjuZDyZqx3q4E

